# M100-C: sensitive-field scan allowlist.
#
# One extended regex per line, matched against "path:lineno" locations.
# - "path:lineno" (e.g. "docs/adr/0012-example.md:42") allows one line.
# - a bare "path" allows every line of that file.
# - "#" lines and trailing "# comments" are ignored.
# Entries must document why the material is safe.

# The scanner script itself defines the detection patterns (BEGIN ... PRIVATE
# KEY, client-*-data:, token formats); self-reference is intentional.
scripts/scan-sensitive-fields.sh

# Change records quote the scanner's own pattern list for documentation.
docs/changes/2026-08-12-m100c-sensitive-field-scan-and-log-redaction.md:16
